  I was playing the other day, and was on a level that looked a little
familiar, somehow, in the way it was set up.  It took me a while to
pin it down, but I finally figured it out; it looked almost exactly
like a Clue board!  This got me to thinking: wouldn't that be a cool
idea for a new level?  You could run into friendly monsters (Col. Mustard,
Professor Plum, etc.), and before you could go down, you would have
to solve the mystery (by #offering it at an altar at the center of the
level).  If your answer is wrong, maybe you lose a point of intelligence.
I haven't thought out the details, but I think it would be a good way
to break away from the mere hack-n-slash that prevails in most of the
game.
 -Tom


